course: dictionary
lesson: 1519
title: Measuring in centimeters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A centimeter is a small unit of length in the metric system. It is about the width of a fingernail, so you can picture it with your own nail.
explain: Ten millimeters make 1 centimeter, and 100 centimeters make 1 meter. Rulers in class show centimeters, so you can check a length with one.
explain: «A rectangle 6 cm long and 4 cm wide holds 4 rows of 6 squares: 6 × 4 = 24 square centimeters.» Here cm is short for centimeter. A square centimeter is the area of a square that is 1 cm on each side.
fact: A centimeter is written cm, for example 6 cm.
fact: 1 meter = 100 centimeters, and 1 centimeter = 10 millimeters.
fact: A «square centimeter» (cm²) measures area, and a «cubic centimeter» (cm³) measures volume.
fact: Centimeters are metric units, and all measurements in science are metric.
exercise: «A rectangle 6 cm long and 4 cm wide holds 4 rows of 6 squares.» What does cm stand for? | meter | *centimeter | kilometer | millimeter
exercise: How many centimeters are in 1 meter? | 10 | 50 | *100 | 1000
exercise: How many millimeters are in 1 centimeter? | 5 | *10 | 100 | 1
test: A rectangle is 6 cm long and 4 cm wide. What is its area in square centimeters? | 10 | 12 | 20 | *24
test: Which unit is best for the width of a fingernail? | meter | hour | *centimeter | kilometer
exam: What is 3 centimeters plus 40 millimeters, in centimeters? | 43 | *7 | 34 | 70
